      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4438_Task5" name="Compliance/Frontend define the SCO item-control policy — age-restricted…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Compliance/Frontend define the SCO item-control policy — age-restricted (cutting tools, solvents/aerosols — profile §5), DG/hazmat (paint/thinners/chemicals — links VS-114), controlled (catch-weight, cut-to-length), and the attendant-intervention requirement
Responsible (R): Compliance / Frontend / DG
Accountable (A): COO / Compliance Lead
Duration: Per policy</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4438_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4438_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4438_Task6" name="IT/Frontend build the intervention flow — SCO flags age/hazmat/controlled item…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: IT/Frontend build the intervention flow — SCO flags age/hazmat/controlled item → attendant ID-verify (age), authorize, weigh/measure (catch-weight VS-115), or block (DG not SCO-eligible), per policy
Responsible (R): IT / Frontend / Compliance
Accountable (A): CIO / COO
Duration: Per design</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4438_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4438_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4438_Task7" name="Compliance/Store train attendants on intervention (ID-check, hazmat handling…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Compliance/Store train attendants on intervention (ID-check, hazmat handling, DG block list), audit adherence (links VS-146), and tune the flag set
Responsible (R): Compliance / Store Ops / LP
Accountable (A): Compliance Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4438_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4438_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4438_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4438_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
