    <bpmn:process id="W_W4440" name="W4440. SCO Acceptance, Change Management &amp; Associate Role Redesign" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: SCO rollout (W4433); workforce planning
Frequency: Per rollout + ongoing
Volume: ~5,800 store staff across 200 stores
Owner: HR/OCM (VS-134/VS-103) / Store Ops (VS-07) / Frontend (VS-08)
Participants: HR (VS-103), OCM (VS-134), Store Ops (VS-07), Frontend (VS-08), L&amp;D (VS-19.4), Labor Relations (VS-84)
Source: workflow W4440 — SCO Acceptance, Change Management &amp; Associate Role Redesign</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4440_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4440_Lane1" name="HR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4440_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4440_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4440_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4440_Lane2" name="Store Ops">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4440_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4440_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4440_Start4" name="SCO rollout (W4433); workforce planning">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4440_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4440_Task5" name="HR/OCM run change management — stakeholder engagement, associate comms (SCO is…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: HR/OCM run change management — stakeholder engagement, associate comms (SCO is role-evolution not replacement), sponsor activation, resistance management (links VS-134)
Responsible (R): HR / OCM / Store Ops
Accountable (A): CHRO / COO
Duration: Per rollout</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4440_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4440_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4440_Task6" name="HR/Frontend redesign the cashier→SCO-attendant role (monitoring, intervention…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: HR/Frontend redesign the cashier→SCO-attendant role (monitoring, intervention, assistance, loss-prevention), retrain (VS-19.4), and manage any labor-relations engagement (VS-84)
Responsible (R): HR / Frontend / L&amp;D / Labor Relations
Accountable (A): CHRO / COO
Duration: Per rollout</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4440_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4440_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4440_Task7" name="Store Ops/HR redeploy freed labor-hours to value-add (assistance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Store Ops/HR redeploy freed labor-hours to value-add (assistance, replenishment, clienteling VS-124) rather than pure reduction, and measure adoption (W4455)
Responsible (R): Store Ops / HR
Accountable (A): COO / CHRO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4440_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4440_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4440_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4440_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4440_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-677 (ensure controlled execution — Self-Checkout &amp; Scan-&amp;-Go Strategy, Design &amp; Technology (PA-149.1).) | - CTL-677: change-managed rollout; role-evolution communicated; labor-relations engaged; freed hours redeployed to value; adoption measured
Owner: HR/OCM (VS-134/VS-103) / Store Ops (VS-07) / Frontend (VS-08)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
